{
  "audioFile": "/audio/marie-curie.mp3",
  "duration": 95.6,
  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.64,
      "text": "Marie Curie is one of the most famous women scientists in history."
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "start": 3.92,
      "end": 7.4,
      "text": "She was born Maria Skladowska in Poland in 1867."
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "start": 7.82,
      "end": 12.36,
      "text": "She became well known for her groundbreaking research on radioactivity and was awarded"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "start": 12.36,
      "end": 13.66,
      "text": "two Nobel Prizes."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "start": 14.3,
      "end": 19.98,
      "text": "In 1903, she shared the Nobel Prize in Physics with her husband Pierre Curie and Henri Becker-El."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "start": 20.18,
      "end": 23.76,
      "text": "In 1911, she received the Nobel Prize in Chemistry on her own."
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "start": 24.0,
      "end": 26.5,
      "text": "She was the first woman ever to win a Nobel Prize."
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "start": 27.5,
      "end": 31.94,
      "text": "From an early age, Marie showed remarkable intelligence and an excellent memory."
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "start": 32.44,
      "end": 37.44,
      "text": "At the age of 16, she received a gold medal for completing her secondary education."
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "start": 38.06,
      "end": 43.46,
      "text": "However, her father lost his savings because of poor investments, so Marie had to work as a teacher."
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "start": 44.08,
      "end": 48.44,
      "text": "She used the money she earned to support her sister Bronia's medical studies in Paris."
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "start": 49.08,
      "end": 52.88,
      "text": "In return, Bronia promised to help Marie pursue her own education later."
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "start": 53.76,
      "end": 60.18,
      "text": "In 1891, Bronia kept his promise and Marie moved to Paris to study at the Sorbonne."
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "start": 60.3,
      "end": 66.3,
      "text": "Now part of the University of Paris, she devoted herself to her studies, often working late into the night."
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "start": 66.46,
      "end": 71.64,
      "text": "Because she had very little money, she survived on a simple diet of bread, butter, and tea."
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "start": 72.4,
      "end": 77.16,
      "text": "Despite these difficult living conditions, she performed exceptionally well in her examinations."
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "start": 77.88,
      "end": 82.66,
      "text": "In 1893, she achieved the highest result in the physical science's examination."
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "start": 83.2,
      "end": 87.1,
      "text": "The following year, she came second in the Mathematical Sciences examination."
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "start": 87.64,
      "end": 95.6,
      "text": "It was not until the spring of 1894 that she met Pierre Curie, who would later become her husband and research partner."
    }
  ],
